    "title": "Brazil vs. Croatia: Time, date, TV channel and how to watch today",
    "text": "March 31, 2026, 2:00 p.m. ETAfter suffering a 2-1 defeat against France in Foxborough, Massachusetts on Thursday, Brazil is looking to bounce back against Croatia on Tuesday in Orlando, Florida.Already dealing with several injury issues, the Seleção were dealt a huge blow as star winger Raphinha sustained a right hamstring injury at Gillette Stadium, ruling him out for five weeks.Carlo Ancelotti's side has gone winless in ots last two friendly matches, with the alarm bells ringing for the winningest nation in World Cup history.Watch Brazil vs. Croatia on FuboMeanwhile, Croatia pulled off an impressive 2-1 victory against Colombia on Thursday in Orlando.Conceding a second-minute goal from Jhon Arias, Croatia's Luka Vušković and Igor Matanović found the back of the net in the first half to seal the victory.In the last matchup between the two nations, Croatia stunned Brazil in the quarterfinals of the 2022 World Cup with a penalty shootout victory.These are the last international friendlies before the final rosters are revealed for the upcoming World Cup, set to begin on June 11.Brazil vs. Croatia prediction, pickAfter defeat to France, Brazil is hoping to end the international break with a victory. While it will definitely be a home match for the five-time world champions in Orlando, Croatia is no stranger to pulling off something incredible against all odds.Prediction: Brazil 1, Croatia 1Brazil vs. Croatia channel, start time, streamingWhen: Tuesday, March 31Where: Camping World Stadium (Orlando, Florida)Time: 8 p.m. ETChannel/streaming: ESPN Deportes (Watch on Fubo), ESPN+ (Watch HERE)Our editors independently choose our recommendations. Some content is produced with paid support from a third party, however our editorial decisions remain independent. If you buy through our links, the USA TODAY Network may earn a commission. Prices and availability may change.",
